  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Alleviating Loneliness Among Migrant Garment Workers in India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With support from Development Innovation Ventures, Good Business Lab Foundation is building off prior pilots to conduct a randomized controlled trial (RCT) of a low-cost mental health intervention that pairs 1,000 female junior factory workers with female senior workers across six factories owned by partner Shahi Exports, India&apos;s largest exporter of ready-made garments. The RCT includes a control group and two intervention groups: one where partners meet a couple times a week to provide general social support and another where senior workers receive specialized training to help junior partners develop strategies to cope with isolation and loneliness. If effective, the intervention has the potential to improve the lives of Shahi&apos;s 150,000 workers in India and Shahi will disseminate the results to its suppliers, partners, other companies, and other organizations working with India&apos;s 120 million rural-to-urban migrant workers.</narrative>
  </description>
